flesler/mcp-files 1.9.0
Enables agents to quickly find and edit code in a codebase with surgical precision. Find symbols, edit them everywhere

Server Usage:
  mcp-files                    # Run MCP server with stdio transport
  TRANSPORT=http mcp-files      # Run MCP server with HTTP transport

CLI Usage:
  mcp-files read_symbol <symbol[,symbol2,...]> <file1> [file2...]  # Find code blocks by symbol name(s)
  mcp-files import_symbol <module_path> [property]                 # Inspect modules and imports  
  mcp-files search_replace <file> <old_text> <new_text>            # Search and replace with whitespace handling
  mcp-files insert_text <file> <from_line> <text> [to_line]       # Insert or replace text at line range (1-based)
  mcp-files os_notification <message> [title]                     # Send OS notifications (title defaults to current directory)
  mcp-files utils_debug                                           # Get debug information

Examples:
  mcp-files read_symbol "ToolConfig" src/types.ts
  mcp-files read_symbol "User,UserService,UserInterface" src/
  mcp-files read_symbol "get*,process*" src/
  mcp-files import_symbol lodash get
  mcp-files search_replace src/app.ts "old code" "new code"
  mcp-files insert_text src/app.ts 10 "console.log('debug')"     # Insert at line 10
  mcp-files insert_text src/app.ts 10 "new code" 12          # Replace lines 10-12
  mcp-files os_notification "Build complete"
